{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall see, and your heart shall rejoice [text should read לבכם].</b> An allusion to the soul, for it is the first chariot." "<b>[And your bones].</b> For they are the foundations." "<b>And wrath.</b> A verb, and the peh always has kamatz and the ayin has patach. If it were mil'el, it would be a noun, and both would have patach."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {0 "The editorial correction לבכם replaces the ketiv לבבכם."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:14.963662172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}